WEBVTT

00:57:58.153 --> 00:58:01.405
don't want to live
in an era of tribal warfare.

00:58:01.429 --> 00:58:02.605
They just don't like it.

00:58:02.629 --> 00:58:04.196
Even in Washington, that's true.

00:58:04.220 --> 00:58:06.850
And so, I have to feel
that we have the ability

00:58:06.874 --> 00:58:08.658
to create an alternative future

00:58:08.682 --> 00:58:11.649
not based on tribe but based on
our commitments to one another.

00:58:11.673 --> 00:58:13.971
CA: I actually love that,
those four words:

00:58:13.995 --> 00:58:15.543
"People figure stuff out."

00:58:15.567 --> 00:58:19.998
But people, actually -- that is
outside most of the discussion.

00:58:20.022 --> 00:58:24.371
Most of the discussion we have
is this sort of dawning realization

00:58:24.395 --> 00:58:28.075
of how awful some new trend
or whatever is,

00:58:28.099 --> 00:58:30.795
and it feels overwhelming to most people.